      "message": "[info] Line 240: The `doOnSuccess { call -\u003e call.setSystemConnection(CALL_ALLOWED_VAL) }` is applied unconditionally to every call routed through `placeCallObservable`, yet the rationale comment scopes it strictly to add-participant calls. The method name is generic, so a future caller reusing `placeCallObservable` for a non-add-participant call would silently bypass Telecom and preempt the real Telecom-driven connection. Consider making the Telecom-bypass intent explicit at the call site (e.g. a dedicated method or a boolean parameter such as `placeAddParticipantCall(...)`) rather than baking it into a generically-named observable, so the bypass can\u0027t be applied unintentionally.",
